1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,750
In this exercise, you were asked to implement a function

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:07,770
that calculates the intersection of a union between two bounding boxes.

3
00:00:07,770 --> 00:00:11,655
Both bounding boxes were defined by four coordinates.

4
00:00:11,655 --> 00:00:18,690
Two, for the upper left corner and two for the lower right corner of the bounding box.

5
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:22,760
First, we need to calculate the coordinates of

6
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:28,145
the bounding box created by the intersection of these two bounding boxes.

7
00:00:28,145 --> 00:00:33,245
We need to keep in mind that these bounding boxes may not intersect,

8
00:00:33,245 --> 00:00:37,800
and this is why I am using the max function here.

9
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:44,720
Then to calculate the union,

10
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:49,685
we need to first calculate the area of both input bounding boxes.

11
00:00:49,685 --> 00:00:52,625
Finally, when calculating the union,

12
00:00:52,625 --> 00:00:57,195
we should not forget to subtract the area of the intersection.

13
00:00:57,195 --> 00:01:04,520
This function is very useful and we will be reusing it in further exercises.

14
00:01:07,290 --> 00:01:10,480
In the second part of this exercise,

15
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:14,605
you were asked to implement a function that calculates precision and

16
00:01:14,605 --> 00:01:20,200
recall for a list of predicted and ground truth bounding boxes.

17
00:01:22,430 --> 00:01:27,010
We can use the numpy.where function to

18
00:01:27,010 --> 00:01:32,245
find where bounding boxes are intersecting with an iou over 0.5.

19
00:01:32,245 --> 00:01:35,590
We can then loop over the values and

20
00:01:35,590 --> 00:01:39,630
compare the ground truth classes with the predicted classes.

21
00:01:39,630 --> 00:01:41,690
If they are equal,

22
00:01:41,690 --> 00:01:43,565
we have a true positive.

23
00:01:43,565 --> 00:01:45,650
But if they are not equal,

24
00:01:45,650 --> 00:01:48,270
we have a false-positive.

25
00:01:50,260 --> 00:01:53,255
To calculate the false negatives,

26
00:01:53,255 --> 00:01:55,520
we first get the number of ground truth

27
00:01:55,520 --> 00:02:00,530
bounding boxes that have not been matched with any predicted bounding boxes.

28
00:02:00,530 --> 00:02:04,280
The false negative are calculated by subtracting

29
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:08,690
this number to the total number of ground truth bounding boxes.

30
00:02:08,690 --> 00:02:16,170
Finally, we use the formula learned in the lesson to calculate precision and recall.

